 * CodeGen objects for the three entities it reshaped (AIPromptRun,
 * ConversationDetail, ConversationCompactionRun). It did not re-bake
 * spDeleteAIAgentRun, whose cascade block SELECTed AIPromptRun.[AgentRunID] and
 * called spUpdateAIPromptRun @AgentRunID = ... to null the FK before deleting
 * the parent row. With the column gone, EVERY AI Agent Run delete failed with
 * "Invalid column name 'AgentRunID'".
 *
 * Why a later `mj codegen` did not self-heal this: cascade-delete regeneration
 * (SQLCodeGenBase.markEntitiesForCascadeDeleteRegeneration) only considers
 * entities whose metadata changed DURING that CodeGen run. The migration
 * updated AIPromptRun's EntityField metadata itself, so a subsequent run saw no
 * change, marked nothing for cascade regeneration, and never re-emitted this
 * procedure. CodeGen did generate the corrected body to disk -- it simply never
 * executed it.
 *
